  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BEL: Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM): migrants in vulnerable situations and refugees in Belarus</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) is a robust field-tested data collection and analysis system that produces critical multi-layered information on migrant profiles, routes, drivers, vulnerabilities, and intentions to enable decision makers and responders provide context specific and effective programmes and policies. DTM will be tasked with the collection of primary data and analysis to generate insights, on the needs, vulnerabilities, intentions and protection challenges of migrants in vulnerable situations and refugees in Belarus. 
Through this intervention, IOM will customize DTM tools and methodologies to the context in Belarus. Taking in account limited official data to inform the data needs of UN agencies to respond to the situation, DTM will provide information on the location, profile, routes, needs and intentions of migrants and refugees. For governmental stakeholders, DTM will enable evidence-based data on profiles of refugees and migrants present in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
